<p>Chinese President Xi Jinping met Kuomintang chairwoman Cheng Li-wun in Beijing on Friday, in the first meeting in nine years between the sitting leaders of China’s Communist Party and Taiwan’s main opposition party, according to multiple reports. Xi said people on both sides of the Taiwan Strait are Chinese and cast peace, development, communication, and cooperation as shared goals, while also saying unification is inevitable or expressing confidence that the two sides would be united. Cheng said the trip was meant to help avoid war and promote peace across the strait, though the visit stirred debate in Taiwan, where critics said she appeared too close to Beijing. Several outlets said the meeting mattered beyond cross-strait messaging. The New York Times reported that Xi used the encounter ahead of a summit with President Trump to present Beijing as a force for stability while increasing pressure on Taiwanese President Lai Ching-te. The broader backdrop is Taiwan’s deep internal divide over how to deal with Beijing: Lai has emphasized deterrence, while the KMT has argued that opposing formal independence and keeping dialogue open can reduce the risk of conflict.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/-iO85fQXb1MIV2zRZ1nBpqhpTIcgfXeBzKjgBmE8AJd7wSgaLHMqteWu4iKSygoYIdMtFiNHw79L_fsGN4dr16t8XgBNYtWrif46DOz63W8wqskHHERQU3I0XQ19BlHoevhVXXRDDaav-_dMRayhFQ_JkE_vaYRgR1K80qwUn8grlOna8u0G_9jjrKaYFKSqVK9ffRzk' alt='News coverage of the meeting between China’s President Xi Jinping and Cheng Li-wun, Taiwan’s Nationalist Party leader, displayed at a restaurant in Beijing, on Friday.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Dormant channel revived: Some outlets described Cheng’s trip as the first by a KMT leader to China in about a decade, reopening senior-level contact that had largely gone quiet.</li><li>Election angle: After the meeting, Cheng said she hoped Xi could visit Taiwan if the KMT wins the island’s 2028 election, underscoring the party’s effort to keep future political channels open.</li><li>Broader security backdrop: The meeting came as Taiwan pushed to strengthen its defenses and shortly after U.S. lawmakers visited the island, showing that peace outreach and deterrence messaging were unfolding at the same time.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Xi Jinping: Xi framed the Taiwan issue around a shared Chinese identity, saying people on both sides of the strait are Chinese and presenting closer ties as a domestic matter rather than a negotiation between separate states. (<a href='https://www.ft.com/content/e4aecf2e-9975-4b44-b01c-d6f2b8435386'>Financial Times</a>)</li><li>Cheng Li-wun and the KMT: Cheng used the visit to argue that the KMT can keep lines open to Beijing, turning the meeting into a demonstration of the party’s dialogue-first approach despite criticism at home. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/china/politics/article/3349617/taiwans-opposition-leader-cheng-li-wun-speaks-after-historic-meeting-xi-jinping'>South China Morning Post</a>, <a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/chinese-president-xi-jinping-kuomintang-kmt-chairwoman-cheng-li-wun-meeting/article70846151.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>President Lai Ching-te: Lai has argued that peace in the Taiwan Strait depends on deterrence — military strength, economic resilience, and coordination with Western and regional partners — not on political accommodation with Beijing alone. (<a href='https://www.rt.com/news/637854-taiwan-china-peace-mission-split/'>RT</a>)</li><li>New York Times analysis: The paper portrayed the encounter as political theater with two aims: undercutting Lai at home while helping Beijing look like the steadier actor to Washington ahead of Xi’s summit with President Trump. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/10/world/asia/taiwan-china-xi-cheng.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/10/world/asia/taiwan-china-xi-cheng.html'>Xi Seeks to Sway Taiwan, and Trump, With Message of Stability</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/chinese-president-xi-jinping-kuomintang-kmt-chairwoman-cheng-li-wun-meeting/article70846151.ece'>Chinese, Taiwanese will unite, Xi Jinping tells Taiwan Opposition leader</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ft.com/content/e4aecf2e-9975-4b44-b01c-d6f2b8435386'>China’s Xi tells Taiwan opposition leader unification an ‘inevitability’</a> - ft.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/china/politics/article/3349617/taiwans-opposition-leader-cheng-li-wun-speaks-after-historic-meeting-xi-jinping'>Cheng hopeful Xi Jinping will visit Taiwan if the KMT wins 2028 election</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/04/10/taiwan-s-opposition-leader-meets-china-s-xi-jinping-as-both-sides-call-for-peace_6752284_4.html'>Taiwan&#x27;s opposition leader meets China&#x27;s Xi Jinping as both sides call for peace</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/news/637854-taiwan-china-peace-mission-split/'>Taiwan splits over One-China: Peace mission challenges war narrative (VIDEO)</a> - rt.com</li></ul>